  "narrative": "No assessments are due, so this explore stage registers follow-ups that should improve generalizability within the supplied dataset while testing a few scientifically plausible new associations. First, I add screen-batch robustness checks for three central validated associations: MSI-high/WRN, KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2, and TP53-loss/USP7, restricted to batch_a. These complement the active batch_a SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 check and the active KY-library MSI-high/WRN check. If the signed estimates remain above the 0.10 clinical-significance benchmark with lower bounds also above it, this strengthens the within-dataset technical consistency of the central findings. If any interval crosses that benchmark, I will interpret that as batch-context uncertainty rather than evidence against the central association, because the central claims are already independently validated. I also register a high-quality matched RNA/DNA plus CRISPR-QC subset check for MSI-high/WRN to see whether the strongest DNA-repair signal persists after excluding cells with incomplete multimodal profile; this is a data-quality robustness check, not an independent validation. Second, I propose new biologically motivated broad probes. BRCA2-deficient cells may depend more strongly on alternative helicase or transcription-related machinery, so I test BRCA2 loss versus stronger DHX9 dependency and stronger POLR2A dependency; the plausible alternative is null or opposite direction if BRCA2 loss creates redundancy rather than increased dependency. KRAS-mutant cells may activate JAK/STAT3-adjacent inflammatory or proliferative signaling, so I test KRAS mutation versus stronger STAT3 dependency. PTEN loss is also tested with STAT3 because PI3K/AKT and STAT3 crosstalk is possible but less predictable; I therefore register an uncertain expectation. Finally, I test EGFR amplification versus TMED10 dependency because EGFR-amplified or receptor-heavy cells could have greater secretory/Golgi-transport load, but this prior is weak. These new claims are all unresolved at registration. The most informative next batch is the batch_a and high-quality subset central robustness checks, followed by the BRCA2, KRAS/STAT3, PTEN/STAT3, and EGFR/TMED10 probes. All conclusions will remain dataset-level associations, not causal mechanisms or claims of external generalizability."
